    <h1>Jixin (Chicken-Heart) Chilli</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The chicken-heart chilli — a small, heart-shaped extra-hot pod at 50,000–70,000 SHU from Guizhou
      and Hunan. The standard for extreme-heat products and Sichuan-style dishes.
    </p>

    <div class="takeaways">
      <strong>Short answer:</strong> Jixin (chicken-heart) is an extra-hot chilli at 50,000–70,000 SHU — among the hottest common Chinese varieties. Because heat is non-linear, it is dosed as an <em>accent</em> by weight: a small dose moves a blend's heat far more than the same weight of a medium chilli.
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What is Jixin chilli?</h2>
    <p>
      Jixin, meaning "chicken heart", is named for its small heart-shaped pod. It sits at the top of
      the common Chinese chilli heat scale at 50,000–70,000 SHU, above the high-heat band — which is
      why it is dosed as an accent rather than a base. See the
      <a href="/heat-levels/extra-hot/">extra hot</a> page for how it fits the 50,000+ band.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Property</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Heat (SHU)</strong></td><td>50,000 – 70,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Region</strong></td><td>Guizhou, Hunan</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Fruit type</strong></td><td>Small, heart-shaped pod</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Best for</strong></td><td>Extreme heat, chilli oil, Sichuan dishes</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What is Jixin pepper used for?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Chilli oil and infused oil</li>
      <li>Sichuan-style and hot-pot dishes</li>
      <li>Extreme-heat seasoning blends</li>
      <li>Snack and instant-noodle heat packs</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">How to specify Jixin chilli</h2>
    <p>
      Name the variety and your target SHU window, then the form — Jixin is commonly supplied as
      segments or powder. Because heat is non-linear, a small dose of Jixin moves a blend's heat far
      more than the same weight of a medium chilli, so dose by weight and confirm the window precisely.
    </p>
    <p class="data-note">
      Heat values are representative per variety. Confirm your exact SHU window and form when you
      inquire.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
