      <h3>What is Jixin chilli?</h3>
      <p>Jixin, the chicken-heart chilli, is a small heart-shaped extra-hot pod at 50,000–70,000 SHU from Guizhou and Hunan. It is a standard for extreme-heat products and Sichuan-style dishes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>How hot is Jixin pepper?</h3>
      <p>Jixin is extra-hot at 50,000–70,000 SHU — among the hottest common Chinese chillies, above the high-heat Sanying and Zidantou band and used where extreme heat is the point.</p>
